/* Modern theme for the generic confirm dialog. #panel's own background/border/box-shadow recipe
   (matching sys_menu.rcss's #panel -- both are small forged-iron dialogs with no hero-banner), the
   shell-edge/groove, and the well's recessed fill all moved to generic_confirm_dialog_bg.rcss --
   see that file's own comment for why (item3D layering). This file is layout/content only now,
   except for `.gcd-header-rail` below -- an in-flow, CSS-painted title banner using Login/SysMenu's
   own header-rail/hero-banner recipes and hardware at their own full size, unlike those two which
   paint their header chrome as part of the shared forged-dialog shell. */

/* #panel is centered via .center-both, not a GetProperty()-read-back calc. dp throughout: a
   LayoutMode::Dialog window (no transform:scale(root_scale)), not one of the root_scale-tracking
   inventory-family windows. Deliberately no paint here -- generic_confirm_dialog_bg.rcss's own
   #panel carries the same width/height so the two documents' panels align exactly. Height is
   160dp + 18dp for the header rail's own full 38dp height (.gcd-body's own top/bottom stay the
   same, so this increase becomes exactly the content area's own gain; bg document's #panel must
   match this exactly). */
#panel {
	width: 230dp;
	height: 178dp;
	font-family: "token(font-body)";
	font-size: 12dp;
	color: token(text-primary);
}
/* Optional taller variant (GenericDialogConfig::tallPanel) -- .gcd-body's own top/bottom insets
   are fixed dp offsets from #panel's edges, so this alone grows .gcd-body/.gcd-content-row/
   .gcd-text-col's available content height for free; the footer/OK/Cancel buttons below need
   their own .tall override since they're positioned via a fixed `top` from #panel's TOP edge.
   250dp grows the ~114dp content well to ~186dp -- enough for a grown .gcd-portrait2d (100x93dp)
   + up to 3 lines, or the numeric-keypad input row, without .gcd-text-col's own scrollbar.
   Mirrored onto the bg document's own #panel imperatively (GenericConfirmDialog.cpp's Show()/
   ShowNext()) since that document has no data model of its own to bind a class through. */
#panel.tall {
	height: 250dp;
}

/* GenericDialogConfig::Portrait2D's own art -- currently always native's IMAGE_MSGBOX_DUEL_BACK
   sprite (newui_DuelWindow.tga), a fixed 148x138 portrait with a caption drawn directly on top --
   the only real consumer today, though Portrait2D itself isn't Duel-specific. A plain, un-skinned
   native asset, so both themes declare the identical rule set for it -- see legacy's own copy of
   this same comment. */
@spritesheet portrait2d-sheet
{
	src: "../../../newui_DuelWindow.tga";
	portrait2d-image: 0px 0px 148px 138px;
}

/* Message well -- layout only (position/overflow/flex); the recessed fill lives in
   generic_confirm_dialog_bg.rcss's .gcd-bg-content-fill instead (same left/right/top/bottom, so
   the fill still lines up exactly behind this box). Text sits directly on it, scrolling
   (overflow: hidden auto) rather than
   growing the panel by default.

   top+bottom (not top+height) deliberately -- this element also has flex centering below, and
   this engine's box model is content-box only (no box-sizing support anywhere in this codebase);
   an explicit height combined with flex/padding on children pushes the box past its intended
   bottom edge. Anchoring both edges keeps the box's outer size exact regardless of content.

   .gcd-content-row is this box's only flex child -- the optional header banner
   (.gcd-header-rail, hidden when untitled) is position:absolute, NOT a flex sibling of it, so it
   doesn't compete with content-row for .gcd-body's own centering (see .gcd-body.has-title below).

   padding is deliberately minimal -- this box's own pre-existing left/right:16dp already plays
   the outer-inset role, and adding more on top double-counts it. Safe to add directly to THIS box
   specifically because it's sized via left/right/top/bottom (anchored edges), not an explicit
   width/height -- padding only shrinks the content area those edges enclose, unlike a
   `width:100%`/`height:100%` child where it would push the box's own outer size past them.
   .gcd-header-rail and .gcd-content-row both inherit the inset via their own width:100%, so this
   insets the whole column, not just the text. */
.gcd-body {
	position: absolute;
	left: 16dp;
	right: 16dp;
	top: 10dp;
	bottom: 54dp;
	padding: 1dp;
	display: flex;
	flex-direction: column;
	justify-content: center;
	align-items: center;
}
/* With a title, .gcd-header-rail moves out of the flex flow entirely (position:absolute below)
   and this reserves its space as padding-top instead (38dp height + 4dp gap) -- content-row is
   then .gcd-body's ONLY flex participant, so its own `justify-content:center` centers content
   within the space actually left after the header, not a [header,content] group centered as a
   unit within the whole box. */
.gcd-body.has-title {
	padding-top: 42dp;
}
/* Optional title banner -- uses base.rcss's own .modern-header-rail paint recipe (copied rather
   than shared since the exact position differs) at its own full, unscaled 38dp height.
   position:absolute (not a flex child of .gcd-body) so it doesn't compete with .gcd-content-row
   for space in .gcd-body's own centering. severity_warning/_error recolor it (warning:
   amber-recolored rail; error: recolored toward .modern-title-plate's own crimson hero-banner
   palette) -- no behavior is gated on them, only styling. */
.gcd-header-rail {
	position: absolute;
	left: 0;
	right: 0;
	top: 0;
	display: flex;
	align-items: center;
	justify-content: center;
	height: 38dp;
	background-color: token(metal-dark);
	decorator:
		linear-gradient(to bottom, rgba(205, 184, 129, 13), transparent 31%),
		linear-gradient(to bottom, token(metal-rail), #171813 45%, token(metal-rail-dark));
	border-width: 1dp;
	border-color: token(border-rail);
	border-bottom-color: #171812;
	box-shadow:
		inset 0 1dp 0 rgba(235, 218, 169, 18),
		inset 0 -1dp 0 #000000,
		0 2dp 4dp rgba(0, 0, 0, 133);
}
/* Cascade-tie fix: .gcd-header-rail sets its own `display`, so an earlier same-specificity
   `.hidden { display: none; }` (base.rcss) loses the tie without this later, more specific
   override. Same fix applies to every other data-class-hidden toggle in this file. */
.gcd-header-rail.hidden { display: none; }
/* Center rivet -- .modern-joint's (base.rcss) own exact values. Plain/warning look only -- hidden
   for severity_error, which uses the twin side studs below instead. */
.gcd-header-joint {
	position: absolute;
	left: 50%;
	top: -8dp;
	width: 13dp;
	height: 13dp;
	margin-left: -6.5dp;
	pointer-events: none;
	background-color: token(metal-groove);
	border-width: 1dp;
	border-color: #484638;
	transform: rotate(45deg);
	box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 2dp #0c0d0b;
}
/* .modern-header-accent's (base.rcss) own exact values. */
.gcd-header-accent {
	position: absolute;
	left: 7dp;
	right: 7dp;
	bottom: 2dp;
	height: 1dp;
	pointer-events: none;
	opacity: 0.35;
	decorator: linear-gradient(to right,
		transparent,
		token(metal-warm-edge) 30%,
		#84754e 50%,
		token(metal-warm-edge) 70%,
		transparent);
}
/* Twin diamond studs -- .login-hero-cap/-left/-right's (login.rcss) own exact values.
   severity_error only, replacing the joint+accent above. */
.gcd-header-cap {
	position: absolute;
	top: 50%;
	width: 11dp;
	height: 11dp;
	margin-top: -5.5dp;
	background-color: #24100a;
	border-width: 1dp;
	border-color: #6a2a19;
	transform: rotate(45deg);
	pointer-events: none;
	box-shadow:
		inset 1dp 1dp 0 rgba(255, 208, 145, 9),
		inset -1dp -1dp 0 rgba(0, 0, 0, 173);
}
.gcd-header-cap-left { left: 8dp; }
.gcd-header-cap-right { right: 8dp; }
.gcd-header-title {
	color: token(text-warm);
	font-family: "token(font-title)";
	font-size: 13dp;
	font-weight: 500;
	letter-spacing: 0.2dp;
	font-effect: shadow(0dp 1dp #000000);
}
.gcd-header-rail.warning {
	border-color: token(semantic-warning);
	box-shadow:
		inset 0 1dp 0 rgba(255, 208, 130, 30),
		inset 0 -1dp 0 #000000,
		0 2dp 4dp rgba(0, 0, 0, 133);
}
.gcd-header-rail.warning .gcd-header-title { color: token(semantic-warning); }
.gcd-header-rail.error {
	background-color: token(metal-title-face);
	decorator:
		linear-gradient(to bottom, rgba(255, 217, 158, 18), transparent 34%),
		linear-gradient(to bottom, #55150f 0%, token(metal-title-face) 56%, token(metal-title-face-dark) 100%);
	border-color: token(border-title);
	box-shadow:
		inset 0 1dp 0 rgba(255, 208, 145, 23),
		inset 0 -1dp 0 #080201,
		0 2dp 5dp rgba(0, 0, 0, 140);
}
/* Distinct brighter gold vs the plain rail's own token(text-warm)/#d6ad45 title -- a color used
   only for this hero-banner look. No existing token matches it exactly, so hardcoded. */
.gcd-header-rail.error .gcd-header-title { color: #e1b94e; }

/* Row holding the item3D anchor + text column, sibling of the header banner (outside .gcd-body's
   own row layout so it doesn't compete with the banner for space). width:100% so it spans
   .gcd-body's full inset width; flex:1 1 auto claims whatever height the (possibly-hidden) banner
   above doesn't. */
.gcd-content-row {
	display: flex;
	flex-direction: row;
	justify-content: center;
	align-items: center;
	width: 100%;
	flex: 1 1 auto;
}
/* Holds lines/input-row/progress-track, alongside #gcd_item3d_anchor within .gcd-content-row.
   Fills .gcd-content-row's full
   height explicitly (rather than relying on align-items, which wouldn't stretch under
   align-items:center) so its own overflow:auto has a real bound to scroll within.

   overflow is `overflow-x, overflow-y` (CSS shorthand order) -- `hidden auto`, NOT `auto hidden`:
   this engine only ever instantiates a scrollbarvertical element when overflow-y is Auto/Scroll,
   never Hidden (Layout/ContainerBox.cpp) -- getting this order backwards silently means no
   scrollbar is ever created, regardless of text length.

   pointer-events: auto is required here too -- base.rcss's `body { pointer-events: none; }`
   inherits down to every descendant that doesn't explicitly opt back in, and the scrollbar's
   generated slidertrack/sliderbar are real DOM children of THIS element, so they inherit whatever
   this element's own computed value is -- without this, the scrollbar can't receive mouse events. */
.gcd-text-col {
	display: flex;
	flex-direction: column;
	justify-content: center;
	align-items: center;
	height: 100%;
	flex: 1 1 auto;
	overflow: hidden auto;
	pointer-events: auto;
}
/* Minimal flat-color scrollbar -- RmlUi generates real child elements for these
   (scrollbarvertical/slidertrack/sliderbar), not pseudo-elements. Arrow buttons collapsed to 0
   size -- drag-only, simplest usable affordance for a narrow well. */
.gcd-text-col scrollbarvertical {
	width: 6dp;
	margin: 0;
}
.gcd-text-col scrollbarvertical slidertrack {
	background-color: token(metal-rail-dark);
}
/* Steel gray, matching .gcd-header-rail's own metal-rail palette rather than the gold accent used
   elsewhere in this dialog -- ties the scrollbar to the header hardware. */
.gcd-text-col scrollbarvertical sliderbar {
	background-color: token(metal-edge);
}
.gcd-text-col scrollbarvertical sliderbar:hover,
.gcd-text-col scrollbarvertical sliderbar:active {
	background-color: token(metal-highlight);
}
.gcd-text-col scrollbarvertical sliderarrowdec,
.gcd-text-col scrollbarvertical sliderarrowinc {
	width: 0;
	height: 0;
}
.gcd-text-col scrollbarhorizontal {
	height: 0;
}
/* font-size/line-height explicit and smaller than #panel's own 12dp default -- deliberately
   subtler than the header title. */
.gcd-line {
	display: block;
	width: 100%;
	text-align: center;
	white-space: normal;
	color: token(text-secondary);
	font-size: 10dp;
	line-height: 15dp;
	font-effect: shadow(0dp 1dp #000000);
}
.gcd-line.bold { font-weight: bold; color: token(text-warm); }

/* Invisible position reference for the native 3D item-preview render pass
   (GenericConfirmDialog.cpp's Render3D()); fixed reference-space size matching
   C3DItemCommonMsgBox's own MSGBOX_3DITEM_WIDTH/HEIGHT (40x40). Renders nothing itself.

   position: static overrides base.rcss's `.layout-anchor { position: absolute; ... }` -- that
   class assumes its own explicit top/left elsewhere, which this anchor doesn't have: it's meant
   to flow as an ordinary flex child of .gcd-body (a row, sibling of .gcd-text-col). */
.gcd-item3d-anchor {
	position: static;
	width: 40dp;
	height: 40dp;
	flex-shrink: 0;
	margin-right: 8dp;
}
/* Cascade-tie fix: this anchor is conditionally hidden (data-class-hidden="!has_item3d") so
   .gcd-text-col alone fills the row when there's no item3D, instead of always reserving a
   40dp-wide empty slot. */
.gcd-item3d-anchor.hidden { display: none; }

/* Optional 2D portrait (GenericDialogConfig::Portrait2D), Overlay layout (the default) -- a
   static flex child INSIDE .gcd-text-col (icon-top/text-below) rather than a sibling like
   .gcd-item3d-anchor (icon-left/text-right, that's the Beside layout below). Same 100x93dp
   sizing as legacy's own copy of this rule -- a plain native asset, not theme-skinned art, so
   it's identical in both themes. */
.gcd-portrait2d {
	position: relative;
	width: 100dp;
	height: 93dp;
	flex-shrink: 0;
	margin-bottom: 4dp;
	decorator: image(portrait2d-image);
}
/* Same cascade-tie fix as .gcd-item3d-anchor above. */
.gcd-portrait2d.hidden { display: none; }
/* Beside layout -- same sizing as legacy's own copy of this rule. */
.gcd-portrait2d-beside {
	position: static;
	width: 60dp;
	height: 56dp;
	flex-shrink: 0;
	margin-right: 8dp;
	margin-bottom: 0;
	decorator: image(portrait2d-image);
}
/* Overlaid directly on the sprite (native draws this ON TOP of the art, not below it) -- matches
   native's own bold yellow; font-effect:shadow keeps it legible over the sprite's bright areas. */
.gcd-portrait2d-text {
	position: absolute;
	left: 0;
	right: 0;
	bottom: 2dp;
	text-align: center;
	font-weight: bold;
	font-size: 9dp;
	color: #ffff00;
	font-effect: shadow(0dp 1dp #000000);
}

/* Optional text-entry field -- see the .rml's own comment for the NumericKeypad-vs-Text split.
   `.btn.gcd-keypad-btn`/`.gcd-keypad-delete` override `.btn`'s own `position: absolute` back to
   static so they can flex-wrap into a grid instead of stacking on top of each other. */
.gcd-input-row {
	display: flex;
	flex-direction: column;
	align-items: center;
	margin-top: 4dp;
}
.gcd-input-row.hidden { display: none; } /* same cascade-tie fix as .gcd-header-rail above */
.gcd-keypad-display {
	color: token(text-warm);
	font-weight: bold;
	letter-spacing: 4dp;
	min-height: 14dp;
	margin-bottom: 4dp;
}
.gcd-keypad-grid {
	display: flex;
	flex-wrap: wrap;
	justify-content: center;
	width: 150dp;
}
.gcd-keypad-grid.hidden { display: none; } /* same cascade-tie fix as .gcd-input-row above */
.btn.gcd-keypad-btn, .btn.gcd-keypad-delete {
	position: static;
	width: 26dp;
	height: 18dp;
	margin: 1dp;
	font-size: 9dp;
}
/* Position reference only, same idea as .gcd-item3d-anchor -- the native g_pSingleTextInputBox
   widget draws on top of this natively, nothing renders through RmlUi here for Mode::Text. */
.gcd-input-anchor {
	position: static;
	width: 150dp;
	height: 18dp;
}

/* Optional progress bar -- same `x_fraction * 100 + '%'` fill technique main_frame.rml's own
   HP/MP/AG/SD/EXP gauges use. */
.gcd-progress-track {
	width: 150dp;
	height: 10dp;
	margin-top: 4dp;
	background-color: token(surface-recessed);
	border: 1dp token(border-inner);
	border-radius: token(radius-sm)dp;
}
.gcd-progress-fill {
	height: 100%;
	background-color: token(accent-gold);
}

/* Divider between the message well and the button row -- base.rcss's .modern-footer,
   repositioned to sit just above the buttons instead of flush with the panel's bottom edge. */
.gcd-footer {
	left: 8dp;
	right: 8dp;
	top: 132dp;
	bottom: auto;
}

/* Three fixed, named-role slots (primary/secondary/cancel -- see GenericDialogConfig's own
   comment). `.gcd-btn-secondary` is a real second action (Decrease/Gift/Discard...), never
   Cancel; `.gcd-btn-cancel` is the always-Cancel/Close slot. Every existing Ok/OkCancel consumer
   always renders solo or paired (primary+cancel), never triple. */
.btn.gcd-btn-primary, .btn.gcd-btn-secondary, .btn.gcd-btn-cancel {
	top: 138dp;
	width: 60dp;
	height: 25dp;
	line-height: 25dp;
}
.gcd-btn-primary   { left: 32dp; }
.gcd-btn-primary.solo { left: 85dp; }
/* Paired: whichever of secondary/cancel is the sole second button sits in this one slot -- both
   selectors share the position since only one is ever visible outside of `.triple`. */
.gcd-btn-secondary, .gcd-btn-cancel { left: 138dp; }
/* Triple (all three shown, e.g. Create/Decrease/Cancel) -- native's own `triwidth = panelWidth/3`
   centering (CUseFruitCheckMsgBox::SetButtonInfo(), CustomMessageBox.cpp), each 60dp button
   centered within its own 230dp/3 = 76.67dp third: primary ~8dp, secondary ~85dp, cancel ~162dp. */
.gcd-btn-primary.triple { left: 8dp; }
.gcd-btn-secondary.triple { left: 85dp; }
.gcd-btn-cancel.triple { left: 162dp; }
/* #panel.tall keeps the same 6dp footer-to-button gap and 15dp button-to-bottom margin the
   default 178dp panel already has (132 -> 204, 138 -> 210, 210 + 25 + 15 = 250). */
#panel.tall .gcd-footer {
	top: 204dp;
}
#panel.tall .btn.gcd-btn-primary, #panel.tall .btn.gcd-btn-secondary, #panel.tall .btn.gcd-btn-cancel {
	top: 210dp;
}
